| OpenXML cleanup: boxing styles, table codes, adjacent runs of one style, line breaks, link bytes
| 1;1 2011-01-04 JES: remove any text contents of boxing styles
| 1;2 2014-01-18 PJS: revise handling of BoxBegin and BoxEnd, leaving
|                     handling of these to wrdpost.sbt

| Preserve any opening boxing style tag, but go to state -1 to delete
| the text contents until a closing tag is encountered.  This logic
| presumes that such tags are always simply paired and not nested.
|028es|~BE-BoxEnd.|031~|028es|~BE-BoxEnd.|031~~-1~(~

| State -1 rules - Delete all until a closing boxing style tag, then
| resume original state.
|028ee|~BE-BoxEnd.|031~|028ee|~BE-BoxEnd.|031~-1~~)~

| htbs codes are created by word2007.xsl with parameters as plain text, e.g:
| <bc:htbs>r:1:0:b:n:a</bc:htbs>
| These rules bring the parameters into the code in binary form, e.g.:
| [bc:htbs;r:1:0:b:n:a]
<bc:htbs>~|028htbs;~1~2~
</bc:htbs>~|031~2~1~

| Combine adjacent runs of ExactTranslation and other styles
| (with or without a single space).
| This is required to fix up .docx files when text in a
| mapped character style is separated into different runs
| due to unique RSID values.
|028ee|~BL-BlockProtectLevel|031 |028es|~BL-BlockProtectLevel|031~ ~
|028ee|~BL-BlockProtectLevel|031|028es|~BL-BlockProtectLevel|031~~
